Okay, stop here. The charisma markup in the normal game is this:

CHA       Price
19+       50%
18        66%
16-18     75%
12-15     100%
10-11      133%
7-9       150%
5-        200%

My patch (charisma.diff) replaces the above with this:
Role      Price
Knight    66%
Healer    66%
other     100%

Now read this: Almost all characters have no (safe) means of increasing
their charisma until far into the game. Therefore, they cannot _use_ it
or _manipulate_ it. They were either born with it or they weren't.
The charisma of most characters is usually 8-14 for most of the time
that it is still relevant (except for Knights and Healers, who always
have at least 16, but usually more.)

All I've done is make the above phenomenon the rule - although my
implementation is, admittedly, slightly skewed toward lower than
expected prices.

>Again, I think you should be finding new uses for Charisma.

This has been said quite a bit, and I welcome any suggestions for new
Charisma applications.



